  V2's honest floor is 4.4% disagreement, against 2.5% for V0 on its own
  null -- the replay has to rerun the draft rollout and the batched verify pass
  itself, and its forward passes do not have the shapes the server's did, so a
  share of acceptance decisions flip on numerics alone. The fix is sound, but it
  is noisier than the detector it replaces.

============================================================================================
3. V1b: share of claimed tokens that PASS the acceptance test
   (attested draft model, uniform from the public position seed)
============================================================================================
             server |  pass rate
---------------------------------
             honest |      95.5%
 honest_spec_seeded |      98.9%
        honest_spec |      96.4%
            seed_43 |      95.5%
       spec_lenient |      93.0%

  The acceptance test passes 95.5% of the wrong-seed ATTACK's tokens and
  95.5% of honest ones. It is a DISTRIBUTIONAL check: it asks whether the
  claimed token was a plausible draw, which is the one thing an output-preserving
  deviation preserves. The cheap spec-aware rung buys nothing against exactly the
  attack that motivated seeded verification in the first place.

  V3 trust_declared: certifies 100% of every server's tokens, without a
  forward pass. A provider asserting `draft = claimed` may name any draft
  probability q_hat <= p(t)/u, so acceptance is forced for every token with
  p(t) > 0. Not measured because it is arithmetic: the disclosure has to be
  RECOMPUTED, not believed.

============================================================================================
What the sound rung costs, per audited sequence (GPU-synchronised)
============================================================================================
  V0 token_difr   one prefill over [prompt+claimed] :    394.9 ms
  V2 spec_replay  re-run the speculative loop       :   4669.1 ms   (11.8x)

  V2 is not a prefill. It replays ~32 sequential rounds, each a
  4-step draft rollout plus a batched target pass, because the round
  structure is only knowable by walking it. The sound spec-aware audit
  therefore costs more than the generation it is checking -- where plain
  recomputation costs one prefill.

